{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And she called to the men of her household.</b> To vindicate herself. However, when she saw that he did not flee outside the room — and this the men of her household also saw — she said to them, <b>and he fled and went outside</b>, as was indeed the case. But to her husband, who had not seen the matter, she said, <b>and he fled outside</b>, to imply that he continued his flight even outside, in order to escape from the men of her household. This was to reinforce the falsehood of her claim." "<b>To make sport of us.</b> In matters of sport, from which it would be apparent that he came to me to lie with me."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:58.645823684Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}